Package: Bergm.ws
Type: Package
Title: Bayesian Multi-Layer ERGMs for Weighted and Signed Weighted
        Networks
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: c(
    person("Alberto", "Caimo", email = "alberto.caimo@gmail.com",
           role = c("aut", "cre"), comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0001-8956-7166")),
    person("Paolo", "Dalena", role = "aut",
           comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0003-2920-9572")),
    person("Isabella", "Gollini", role = "aut",
           comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0002-7738-5688")))
Description: Bayesian hierarchical multi-layer dissolution exponential random
    graph models for weighted and signed weighted networks. A weighted network
    is decomposed into nested binary layers by thresholding its edge weights,
    and each transition between consecutive layers is modelled conditionally on
    the observed lower layers: on the layers alone with bergm_w(), or jointly
    with the edge signs with bergm_ws(). Layer-specific parameters are
    partially pooled through a Normal-inverse-Wishart hierarchical prior and
    estimated with an adaptive approximate exchange algorithm: joint or
    layer-wise updates, delayed acceptance with a Gaussian approximation of the
    likelihood, the hierarchical mean integrated out of the exchange step, and
    a proposal covariance initialised from the Fisher information, learned
    during the burn-in and pooled across chains. The package also provides a
    model builder that checks that every statistic is computed on its own
    layer, prior and posterior predictive checks with goodness-of-fit
    statistics not used in the model, convergence diagnostics and a check of
    the length of the auxiliary chains.
